  "request": "Which classes inherit from ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/models.py) only indirectly, i.e. through at least one intermediate class of this repository, and do not name ApiModel directly in their class statement? An import alias of ApiModel (auto_ontology/server/responses.py imports it as _Payload) counts as naming ApiModel directly, and a subscripted base such as ListResponse[T] counts as its class. For each, give the class symbol ID and the length of the shortest inheritance chain to ApiModel (2 when the parent class directly subclasses ApiModel).\n\nRequested output columns: class_symbol_id (string), depth (integer).",
  "explanation": "The query uses a recursive CTE to traverse the inheritance graph starting from classes that directly subclass ApiModel (depth 2). It then finds classes that inherit from those intermediate classes, incrementing depth by 1 each level, while excluding ApiModel from intermediate steps and avoiding duplicate processing. The result lists all indirectly inherited classes with their shortest chain length to ApiModel.",
  "sql": "WITH RECURSIVE inheritance_tree AS (\n  -- Base case: classes that directly subclass ApiModel\n  SELECT s.symbol_id AS class_symbol_id, 2 AS depth\n  FROM code.symbols s\n  JOIN code.class_bases cb ON s.symbol_id = cb.class_symbol_id\n  WHERE cb.base_name = 'ApiModel'\n\n  UNION ALL\n\n  -- Recursive case: find classes that subclass intermediate classes\n  SELECT s.symbol_id, it.depth + 1\n  FROM inheritance_tree it\n  JOIN code.class_bases cb ON cb.base_symbol_id = it.class_symbol_id\n  JOIN code.symbols s ON cb.class_symbol_id = s.symbol_id\n  WHERE cb.base_name != 'ApiModel'  -- exclude ApiModel itself from intermediate\n  AND s.symbol_id NOT IN (SELECT class_symbol_id FROM inheritance_tree)\n)\nSELECT class_symbol_id, depth\nFROM inheritance_tree\nORDER BY depth, class_symbol_id",
